From 878eb73242b2118ff0ca22e540d4f81e6fe44f0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 01:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 45/52] ppc32: answer maglev's CpuOperation::kFloat64Round
 query for the 32-bit target

G5 build error #7a of the 12.4 port (maglev-graph-builder.cc; the
user worked around it on the G5 so the build could reach the link
step, this commit is the series' version of that fix).

The harness compiles six src/maglev TUs even with Maglev codegen off,
because Turboshaft's maglev-graph-building-phase reaches into the
graph builder unconditionally (BUILD.gn:5141).  The graph builder's
IsSupported(CpuOperation) ladder lists every backend that answers the
kFloat64Round query and #errors for anything else; V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC
(ppc32) was not in it.

Answer false: the ppc32 backend advertises
MachineOperatorBuilder::kNoFlags (the round ops need frim/frip/friz/
frin, ISA 2.02+, which the G3/G4/G5 lack), so the same answer the
Turbofan pipeline already gets from SupportedMachineOperatorFlags.
The query is only reachable through the maglev graph builder, which
runs on this target only if --turboshaft-from-maglev is ever turned
on; the false answer keeps that path on the builtin-call fallback the
backend can actually execute.  PPC64 keeps its place in the
return-true branch above (matched first in the #elif chain).
---
 v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc b/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc
index 3b99a44..6bae2e3 100644
--- a/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc
+++ b/v8/src/maglev/maglev-graph-builder.cc
@@ -79,6 +79,12 @@ bool IsSupported(CpuOperation op) {
     defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_RISCV32) || defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_LOONG64) || \
     defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_MIPS64)
       return true;
+#elif defined(V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC)
+      // ppc32: the backend advertises kNoFlags (frim/frip/friz/frin are
+      // ISA 2.02+, absent on the G3/G4/G5 cores; see
+      // InstructionSelector::SupportedMachineOperatorFlags), so the
+      // rounding operations are not available as machine ops here either.
+      return false;
 #else
 #error "V8 does not support this architecture."
 #endif
